# A `break` out of `for (const value of list)` is a plain edge out of the loop: there is no iterator to close. An element costs one load and two branches: the test of the body and the test of the counter.
# The first loop that is printed only asks again which storage the array has, behind a rare edge. The second one walks the elements.
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK: Double b@[[value]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedDoubleProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isNegative]] = LessThan(b@[[value]], $0.000000(
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNegative]], Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0, {{*}} steps by 1
